<rml>
<head>
    <title>Update</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="tokens.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="case.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="mark.rcss"/>
</head>
<body class="overlay">
    <!-- The update plate (the user's ask of 2026-09-23: "it must show an overlay that an update
         is available, it can download in bg and say to the user the new update will install next
         restart"). The counter's plate, at the BOTTOM left so it sits under neither corner plate
         and never under the title bar. It appears only while there is something to say: the newer
         version being fetched, the fetched file verified and waiting for the next start, or a
         download that failed verification and was deleted. A click while the file is ready
         installs it now and closes this copy, which is what F5 does. -->
    <div class="counter update" id="update">
        <div class="mark"></div>
        <span class="counter-value" id="update-value">Update</span>
        <span class="counter-unit" id="update-note"></span>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
